  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n7 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes} = 70 \\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince 70 is less than the 100 shrimp available, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is less than the 100 available, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60 \\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nShe discards 5 damaged shrimp afterward:\n\n\\[\n60-5=\\boxed{55\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]\n\nSo she peels 60 shrimp, of which 55 remain.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp. After discarding 5 damaged shrimp, \\(55\\) remain.\n\nHer sautéing rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp per minute}\n\\]\n\nIn 10 minutes, she can sauté:\n\n\\[\n2.5 \\times 10=25\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, assuming peeling and sautéing can occur during the same ten-minute period, she can fully prepare:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp. After discarding 5 damaged shrimp, \\(55\\) remain.\n\nShe can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in 10 minutes, so the limiting amount is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily works sequentially, each shrimp requires both peeling and sautéing time.\n\n- Peeling rate: \\(6\\) shrimp/minute, so peeling takes \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute per shrimp.\n- Sautéing rate: \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes \\(=3\\) shrimp/minute, so sautéing takes \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute per shrimp.\n\nLet \\(x\\) be the number of shrimp she successfully sautés. She must also peel the \\(5\\) damaged shrimp, so she peels \\(x+5\\) shrimp total.\n\nThe total time is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x+5}{6}+\\frac{x}{3}\\le 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx+5+2x\\le 60\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3x\\le 55\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx\\le 18\\frac{1}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, she can fully peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s rates are:\n\n- Peeling: \\(6\\) shrimp per minute\n- Cooking: \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes \\(=3\\) shrimp per minute\n\nTo end up with \\(90\\) cooked shrimp, she must peel \\(95\\) shrimp because \\(5\\) are discarded:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Peeling time}=\\frac{95}{6}=15\\tfrac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cooking time}=\\frac{90}{3}=30\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSince she works sequentially:\n\n\\[\n15\\tfrac{5}{6}+30=45\\tfrac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, it will take Emily\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45\\tfrac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nor \\(45\\) minutes and \\(50\\) seconds.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
